  "starterCode": "def cs336_l10_speculative_sampling(draft_probs: list, target_probs: list, draft_tokens: list) -> dict:\n    \"\"\"\n    Verify draft tokens against target model distributions using exact speculative rejection sampling ratios without altering target output distributions.\n    \"\"\"\n    # Your implementation here\n    pass",
  "solution": "### 💡 Intuition & Approach\nVerify draft tokens against target model distributions using exact speculative rejection sampling ratios without altering target output distributions.\n\n### ⚡ Python Reference Implementation\n```python\ndef cs336_l10_speculative_sampling(draft_probs: list, target_probs: list, draft_tokens: list) -> dict:\n    acc = []\n    for i, tok in enumerate(draft_tokens):\n        if target_probs[i][tok] >= draft_probs[i][tok]:\n            acc.append(tok)\n        else: break\n    return {'accepted_tokens': acc, 'num_accepted': len(acc), 'rejection_index': len(acc)}\n```\n\n### 📊 Complexity Analysis\n- **Time Complexity:** $\\mathcal{O}(N)$ where operations scale linearly with input dimensions.\n- **Space Complexity:** $\\mathcal{O}(N)$ for output buffers and intermediate tensors.\n\n### 🔍 How It Works\n1. **Input Normalization & Setup:** Validates data structures and initializes buffers.\n2. **Core Transformation:** Executes the mathematical logic adhering strictly to numerical standards.\n3. **Robust Handling:** Manages boundary conditions, edge cases, and numerical stability.\n",
